      "writtenOn": "2023-09-04T16:56:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we actually need to include this in the API \u0026 the AIDL service?\nIt means a lot of churn when we add \u0026 remove flags.\nWe could just hardwire the string at the isFeatureEnabled call site.\nA typo could lead to a feature not being used when it is enabled, but not vice versa which would be more harmful.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 102,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 120,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "fd0c9a45b339f9572696b3a62b48d3ad4b7e6d52",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "88ea5434_665a53ae",
        "filename": "javalib/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachineManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 120,
      "author": {
        "id": 1432579
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-04T21:21:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need this to be at least @TestApi unless we want our CTS tests to build against hidden APIs, which I think is a bad idea.\n\n\u003e We could just hardwire the string at the isFeatureEnabled call site.\n\nDo you mean in the test itself? Or implement isFeatureEnabled entired in VirtualMachineManager? The former I think won\u0027t work because the CTS binary is built separately from the device images. If it is the later, then it will take sometime to implement, and I was thinking of doing it as a long term solution once build time flags support is more mature.\n\n\u003e A typo could lead to a feature not being used when it is enabled, but not vice versa which would be more harmful.\n\nWith the current approach an engineer need to define a constant in one place (IVirtualizationService.aidl), and reference it other places (VirtualMachineManager.java for @TestApi constant), and virtualizationmanager/src/aidl.rs for the check. I think the only place where the typo can occur is the src/aidl.rs (check against a wrong cfg), and unfortunately we will need to be careful for the time being.\n\nNote: this change is just to unblock folks for writing CTS tests against their flag-guarded features, while we figure out the more scalable approach. Does this make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "4ed0c0fc_9d7296be",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 102,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 120,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "fd0c9a45b339f9572696b3a62b48d3ad4b7e6d52",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
